# Modelfile.fast -- sim-fast (MODEL_FAST)
#
# Provenance: FROM the registry-pulled `llama3.2:3b` (Q4_K_M, ~2 GB), NOT
# the LM Studio-cached beehive-lab FP16 GGUF. Phase 0 rejected that cached
# file (see "Ollama Phase 0 findings (2026-07-24)" in TASKS_PENDING.md,
# finding #8/#9): it is FP16 (~2.4x the VRAM/compute of a Q4 quant, ~8 GB
# resident alone) and its embedded chat template leaks raw ChatML stop
# tokens (`<|im_end|>`, `<|fim_end|>`) into `content` on some prompts --
# unacceptable for the PIANO module / summarizer / meta-system outputs this
# tier serves. `ollama pull llama3.2:3b` gets Meta's own quant with a clean,
# matching Llama 3.2 template instead. `FROM llama3.2:3b` in a Modelfile
# layers on that already-pulled registry model (verified working in
# Ollama 0.32.3) rather than re-downloading blobs.
#
# num_ctx 4096: this tier serves one-sentence/one-number PIANO module,
# summarizer/wiki-merge, and meta-system prompts (~1k tokens per Phase 0's
# plan estimate) -- see ollama_config.md for the budget table.
#
# Sampling params mirror simulation/server.py's NON_THINKING_SAMPLING dict
# (top_p 0.8, top_k 20, min_p 0) plus the lm_complete() default temperature
# (0.5, the background-cognition entry point that always routes to
# MODEL_FAST). Same caveat as Modelfile.smart: server.py sends its own
# per-request `options` which win over these; this just keeps standalone/
# manual invocations consistent.
#
# NO SYSTEM directive -- see Modelfile.smart's note; Phase 6 territory only,
# and only applies to sim-smart per the migration plan (the load-time
# rulebook is the elder/decision system prompt, not the module prompts this
# tier serves).
#
# Canonical applier: scripts/ollama_setup.py (`ollama create sim-fast -f
# ollama/Modelfile.fast`, idempotent). The script also `ollama pull
# llama3.2:3b` first if the base model is missing.

FROM llama3.2:3b

PARAMETER num_ctx 4096
PARAMETER temperature 0.5
PARAMETER top_p 0.8
PARAMETER top_k 20
PARAMETER min_p 0
